---
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import Todo from '../components/Todo.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="This website sets no cookies and uses no analytics or tracking. What is stored on your device, and how Moodle, giscus and email work."
  lead="This website sets no cookies and uses no analytics or tracking. This page explains the few places where data is involved."
  prose
>
  <p class="meta">Last updated 5 October 2026.</p>

  <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No cookies, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking pixels.</li>
    <li>Fonts and all other files are served from wosm.academy itself, so visiting a page sends no requests to other services. The one exception is comments on Journal posts, described below.</li>
    <li>
      Two small preferences are kept in your browser’s local storage, if you set them: your choice of light or dark
      theme (<code>wosm:theme</code>) and whether the background animation is paused (<code>wosm:sim-paused</code>).
      They never leave your device. Clearing your browser’s site data removes them.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub states that when a GitHub Pages site is visited, the visitor’s IP
    address is logged and stored for security purposes. See <ExternalLink
      href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection"
      >GitHub Pages: data collection</ExternalLink
    > and the <ExternalLink
      href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
      >GitHub General Privacy Statement</ExternalLink
    >. We do not receive these logs.
  </p>

  <h2 id="journal-comments">Journal comments and reactions</h2>
  <p>
    Journal posts have comments and reactions provided by giscus, which stores them as GitHub Discussions. Nothing is
    loaded from giscus until you scroll to the comments at the end of a post; then your browser connects to giscus.app
    and GitHub. To comment or react you sign in with your GitHub account and authorise giscus, which keeps an encrypted
    token in your browser’s local storage. Your comments are public on GitHub. See the <ExternalLink
      href="https://github.com/giscus/giscus/blob/main/PRIVACY-POLICY.md">giscus privacy policy</ExternalLink
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 id="moodle">Moodle (moodle.wosm.academy)</h2>
  <p>
    Courses are taught on our Moodle site, which is a separate service. When you create an account there, Moodle stores
    the details you give it (such as your name and email address) and your activity in courses.
    {
      site.moodle.privacy ? (
        <>
          See <ExternalLink href={site.moodle.privacy}>Moodle’s privacy policy</ExternalLink>.
        </>
      ) : (
        <Todo>link to the privacy policy page on moodle.wosm.academy</Todo>
      )
    }
  </p>

  <h2 id="email">Email and teaching applications</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your address and your message and use them only to reply. If you apply to teach, we use
    your CV and letter only to consider your application. <Todo
      >how long applications are kept and when they are deleted</Todo
    >
  </p>

  <h2 id="discord">Discord</h2>
  <p>
    Our community server runs on Discord, which has its own <ExternalLink href="https://discord.com/privacy"
      >privacy policy</ExternalLink
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Questions and your rights</h2>
  <p>
    For any question about your data, or to ask us to correct or delete data we hold about you, email <a
      href={`mailto:${site.email.general}`}>{site.email.general}</a
    >. <Todo>who is responsible for personal data (the data controller) and the applicable law</Todo>
  </p>
  <p>If we ever add analytics, it will be cookieless and privacy-respecting, and this page will say so first.</p>
</PageLayout>
